---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import { release, releaseNote } from '../data/release';

const app = 'https://github.com/albertoarena/sudo-play';
---
<Base title="Install" description="How to get Sudo Play onto your Mac, where its releases are published, and how to run it from source today.">
  <h1>Install</h1>
  <p class="lead">Sudo Play is a menu bar app for macOS. {releaseNote()}</p>

  {!release && (
    <>
      <p>The first release will be a signed DMG attached to a GitHub Release, so it opens without a security warning. Releases are on the app's <ExternalLink href={`${app}/releases`}>releases page</ExternalLink>.</p>
      <h2>Until the first release</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Hear when it ships.</strong> On the app's <ExternalLink href={app}>GitHub page</ExternalLink>, choose Watch, then Custom, then Releases. GitHub tells you when the first DMG is out.</li>
        <li><strong>Add a playlist.</strong> Anyone can add one to the catalog with a pull request. The contributing guide explains how, in <ExternalLink href={`${app}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#adding-a-playlist`}>Adding a playlist</ExternalLink>.</li>
      </ul>
    </>
  )}

  {release && (
    <>
      <h2 id="download-and-install">Download and install</h2>
      <p>You need a Mac with Apple silicon, M1 or later, and the Spotify app or a browser. There is no Intel build yet.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Download</strong> <ExternalLink href={release.dmg.url}>{release.dmg.file}</ExternalLink> ({release.dmg.size}) from the <ExternalLink href={release.url}>{release.name} release</ExternalLink>.</li>
        <li><strong>Install.</strong> Open the DMG and drag Sudo Play to Applications.</li>
        <li><strong>Open</strong> Sudo Play. macOS asks once whether to open an app downloaded from the internet. Click <strong>Open</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>The first time you press Play, macOS asks whether Sudo Play may control Spotify. Click Allow, so it can start the playlist in the Spotify app.</p>
      <p><strong>Coming from an earlier version?</strong> Download the DMG and drag Sudo Play to Applications, then choose Replace. Your settings stay. The app does not update itself.</p>

      <h2>Check the download</h2>
      <p>This step is optional. In Terminal, run:</p>
      <pre><code>shasum -a 256 ~/Downloads/{release.dmg.file}</code></pre>
      <p>It should print <code>{release.dmg.sha256}</code>.</p>

      <h2>Hear about new releases</h2>
      <p>On the app's <ExternalLink href={app}>GitHub page</ExternalLink>, choose Watch, then Custom, then Releases. Sudo Play does not check for updates itself, because the daily catalog download is its only network call.</p>
    </>
  )}

  <h2 id="run-it-from-source">Run it from source</h2>
  <p>You can also run Sudo Play on a Mac with PHP 8.4, Composer and Node 22 or later. The app's README has the steps, in <ExternalLink href={`${app}#run-it-from-source`}>Run it from source</ExternalLink>. A copy of the catalog ships with the app, so it has playlists to suggest from the first run, even offline.</p>
</Base>
